course: dictionary
lesson: 8753
title: One word, many meanings: settle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and settle is one of them. It can mean to come to rest, to calm down, to decide, to live in a new place, or to pay. The sentence tells you which meaning is right, so read the words around settle before you choose.
explain: «Dust settles on the shelves» means the dust comes to rest and stays there. «Settle the bill» is different: it means pay what you owe. Ask yourself what is being settled. Dust cannot pay, so settle here cannot mean pay.
explain: Try the swap test. Put a simple word in place of settle and check that the sentence still makes sense. «Llamas spit mostly at each other to settle arguments» works with end: they spit to end arguments. Settle means end here.
fact: Settle is a verb: settle, settles, settled, settling.
fact: «Settle down» means become calm and quiet, as a class does when the teacher asks.
fact: «Settle in» means get used to a new place, like «the family settled in Canada».
fact: «Settle an argument» means end it, often by finding a fair answer.
fact: Settlers who settle a place build settlements, which are villages and towns.
exercise: «Dust settles on the shelves.» What does settles mean here? | To cook slowly | To shout loudly | To run away fast | * To come to rest and stay
exercise: «They spit mostly at each other to settle arguments.» What does settle arguments mean? | To cook them | To write them down | * To end them | To start them
exercise: The teacher says, «Please settle down.» What does she want the class to do? | * To be calm and quiet | To run around the room | To sing as loudly as they can | To go home early
test: «The family settled in Canada.» What does settled in mean? | To leave Canada forever | To build a boat | * To move to a new place and live there | To pay for a holiday there
test: «Ruby's teacher showed three questions that settle almost any claim.» What does settle mean? | To bury something | To pay a bill | To sit down quietly | * To decide or prove something
exam: «Ella had to settle the bill at the café.» What does settle mean here? | To ask for the menu | * To pay what she owed | To leave a tip only | To sit down and wait
